        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-12-04T00:11:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idea is configuration happens independantly of creating an instance.  This was specifically asked for by adam young (and I agree with him) that the object instantiation should happen independently of configuration since the configuration is ostensibly quite complex and fairly orthogonal to the object.  This is similar to how dogpile works.  It allows for configuration to happen after other work has been done, but not have it strongly tied to the instantiation.\n\nThis does bring up another issue, making sure it is configured before use.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAATn/99zc\u003d",
      "revId": "4b91f56fafce50619cdf26370cb851b40838587e",
