    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAATn/99u0\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/kvs/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 7725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-12-03T23:25:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do you need to lock here? I would expect the backend to serialize access to a key already. Does that not happen for one of the backends?",
      "revId": "4b91f56fafce50619cdf26370cb851b40838587e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAATn/99fE\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/kvs/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-12-04T00:11:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The mutex for locking is handled at this layer, you can\u0027t lock in the backend, and this is designed to ensure we can perform a nearly-transactional update for a case of updating a user_token_list (or similar) that previously was relying on the CAS (memcache compare and set) mechanism.  Instead of trying to set and failing because the CAS_ID changed, we wrap in a lock and perform the get, update, set in a single locked context.\n\nThis could probably go away if we never want to lock sets (let races happen unless you wrap the set in a lock context).  Input on the approach is welcome.  But if we remove this very active systems might have a delete go through after a set occurs.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAATn/99u0\u003d",
      "revId": "4b91f56fafce50619cdf26370cb851b40838587e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAATn/99uc\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/kvs/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 370,
      "author": {
        "id": 7725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-12-03T23:25:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s the race condition here?",
      "revId": "4b91f56fafce50619cdf26370cb851b40838587e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAATn/99dE\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/kvs/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 370,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-12-04T00:11:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is more of a mirror of previous \"workings\" where an attempted delete would raise an exception.  In the case of the new delete, we want to ensure that functionality is still met, so we lock and get (raises not found if it doesn\u0027t exist) and then performs the delete.  It\u0027s about communicating back to the rest of the system that the item doesn\u0027t exist rather than silently failing or attempting to perform a delete on a non-existant value that gets set elsewhere.\n\nMost uses of the context here are edge-cases on very busy systems.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAATn/99uc\u003d",
      "revId": "4b91f56fafce50619cdf26370cb851b40838587e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    }
